quiz.q:
This function should print the user name part of an e-mail address (the text before the `'@'`), but it crashes on some inputs. Explain why, and fix it so that it prints `no @` when there is none.

```c
void print_user(const char *email) {
    const char *at = strchr(email, '@');
    printf("%.*s\n", (int) (at - email), email);
}
```

(`%.*s` prints at most that many chars of the string.)

quiz.answer:
When there is no '@', `strchr` returns `NULL` and `at - email` subtracts with a null pointer: undefined behaviour. Fix: test first.

```c
if (at == NULL) {
    printf("no @\n");
    return;
}
```

and only then print.

